    "result_text": "Done. The build succeeds and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an `initials` field returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}` that yields the upper-cased first letters of firstName and lastName, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\n**Two changes, chosen to minimize structural impact:**\n\n1. **`Person.java`** \u2014 added a new small, self-contained `getInitials()` method (CC 1). I placed it on `Person` rather than `Owner` because `Person` has very low surrounding complexity (only four trivial getters/setters), so the `WMC_other` cost is small \u2014 versus `Owner`, which carries many methods. `initials` derives from `firstName`/`lastName`, which live on `Person`, so it's the natural home too.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `initials` property to the `Owner` schema so the OpenAPI generator emits it on `OwnerDto`.\n\n**No mapper change needed:** MapStruct auto-maps `Owner.getInitials()` \u2192 `OwnerDto.initials` by property name, so `OwnerMapper` and all the function/YAML wiring stayed untouched. Two files touched, one new trivial function.",
